{"ts":"2026-10-23T05:20:50.174304042Z","session":"837b52b4-d41d-4919-9e09-c68083ddd2a3","agent_id":"a18d72123d07b39a2","agent_type":"invariant-completeness-reviewer","tool":"SubagentHandback","tool_input":{"message":"Review of d85107b against docs/design-opencode-plugin.md, DESIGN.md, docs/spec-opencode-lifecycle.tex and .tmp/lc3/r6. I found five things to fix: one in the sweep-coverage list, one in the DESIGN.md sentence you asked about, two coverage-wording points, and one gap in the spec's older coverage paragraph. Checks 2, 3 and 4 hold.\n\n**How I checked the runs.** A row's slice is the set of operation schemas present in its `.tex`. I took the files that define all three of `\\begin{schema}{LcCloseUnlockedBegin}`, `{LcSweepWrite}` and `{LcCfExitNoRetry}`. That set is: every U1_* and U2_* row (27, including U1_leak_d3), F2_* (7), F3_* (6), Fv2_on, Fv2_off, Fc_w, Fc_del, five C16 mutants (MutResumeCas, MutResumeCas_leak, MutResumeKeepRec, MutResumeKeepRec_wf, MutResumeNoCloseSkel), MutCasFresh, and R1_cex.\n\n- Every U*_all row and U1_leak_d3 has all 16 `fix*` switches set to `ztrue`, and its `.out` says \"ALL states visited\".\n- F2_* stops at 200,000 states and F3_* at 40,000 (depth 5); both say \"not all states visited\". Fv2_on stops at 300,000.\n- No row outside the U slices both has all sixteen switches on and exhausts its space, apart from mutants. So the \"exhaustively … only on claim-u and claim+u\" half of the sentence holds.\n- R1_cex is not in the spec table (it duplicates MutResumeNoCloseSkel: 8,744 states, depth 12), so it needs no mention.\n\n**Findings**\n\n1. **MEDIUM — Fv2_off is missing from the \"also contain both\" list.**\n   - Where: design-opencode-plugin.md:1540-1541 (\"the counterexample rows `Fc_w` and `Fc_del` also contain both\") and DESIGN.md:12622-12623 (same list).\n   - Falsifying case: Fv2_off.tex contains all three schemas and is a table row (spec:2441: all but Cas, counterexample, verdict slice, 5,838 states). The list names the bounded and counterexample rows outside the U slices, so it reads as complete.\n   - Fix: add Fv2_off to the counterexample rows in both files. The U*_off rows (all but ResumeClosed) also contain both, but they are on the named claim-u/claim+u slices; adding \"and the U*_off rows\" would close that too.\n\n2. **MEDIUM — DESIGN.md:12627-12637 calls the id counter \"not represented\".**\n   - The sentence lists \"the id counter\" under \"Also not represented:\", then says every operation leaves `used` unchanged or grows it. That second clause says the counter is in the model.\n   - What N20 actually excludes is the code's `releaseID(false)` returning an id, and the timing of consumption.\n   - Fix: list \"an id returned to the counter (`releaseID`)\" as the thing not represented, then give the `used` argument as the reason uniqueness holds in the model.\n\n3. **MEDIUM — the N20 argument omits the premise that makes ids unique.**\n   - Where: spec:2912-2914, design:1584-1585, DESIGN.md:12632-12634.\n   - Growing `used` and starting it empty do not on their own make ids unique. Uniqueness needs both allocators to refuse an id already used: `d? \\notin used` (spec:1377 in `LcCfAlloc`, spec:1706 in `LcTierBDispatch`).\n   - The schema claim itself holds. Every other `\\Delta Lifecycle` schema includes `\\Xi LcUsed`, and Init (545), LcInitChain (579) and LcInitPair (612) set `used' = \\emptyset`. No `\\defs` composite touches `used`.\n   - Fix: add \"and each allocates only an id not in `used`\".\n\n4. **MEDIUM — \"also contain both\" can be read as \"exercised both\".**\n   - Where: design:1540-1541, DESIGN.md:12622.\n   - \"Contain\" is literally true: the schemas are in the slice. But the `.out` files show operations never fired: F3_* end at \"7 operations not covered\", F2_* at 3, Fc_w and Fc_del at 2.\n   - The output does not name which operations, so I could not confirm that `LcCfExitNoRetry` or `LcCloseUnlockedBegin` ever fired in those rows. Fv2_on reports ALL OPERATIONS COVERED.\n   - Fix: say \"contain both schemas\" and state that the bounded rows do not cover every operation, or check coverage per operation.\n\n5. **MEDIUM — the spec's coverage-gap paragraph now disagrees with the design.**\n   - Where: spec:2690-2696 (\"The gap that let C16 through\").\n   - It lists the slices holding the unlocked sweep (claim, claim+, sweep, verdict, full machine) and omits sweep+ensure. Fc_w and Fc_del (spec:2437-2438, slice sweep+ensure) contain the sweep and `LcCfExitNoRetry`, which the design now states.\n   - Fix: add sweep+ensure to the paragraph (\"had both but was run only for `SweepComplete` with the switches off or DeleteCloses alone, and found counterexamples\").\n\n**Checks that hold**\n\n- **Check 2 (new-row description, spec:2370-2372).** The 33 new rows are the 27 U rows (13 U1, 13 U2, U1_leak_d3), the 5 C16 mutants, and MyRelKeepRec. That matches rows5new.txt (32) plus rowsRel.txt (1). rows5old.txt has 97 rows, and the table has 130 rows. MyRelKeepRec is described as the release mutant of N18, consistent with spec:2901.\n- **Check 3 (C16 close failure).** design:247 and design:1166-1167 say \"write failed\". The write-failed table row (design:2298) covers \"the close that the closed-mission exit performs first (C16)\". The do-not-retry row (design:2299), design:2185-2188, DESIGN.md:12319-12322 and 12354-12356, and spec:2177-2186 and 2795-2799 all keep the record and do not assign this case \"do not retry\". No remaining place does.\n- **Sweep-coverage sentence.** \"All sixteen switches\" matches the 16 `fix*` constants (spec:187-202).\n\nThe commit introduced no other false statement."},"tool_input_hash":"1befe3c52fc22333bba819d666184fd2138d4bb8d8bcbbc7cb3b569deba285dd","tool_input_preview":"{\"message\":\"Review of d85107b against docs/design-opencode-plugin.md, DESIGN.md, docs/spec-opencode-lifecycle.tex and .tmp/lc3/r6. I found five things to fix: one in the sweep-coverage list, one in th..."}
{"ts":"2026-10-23T05:21:00.703067603Z","session":"837b52b4-d41d-4919-9e09-c68083ddd2a3","tool":"SendMessage","tool_input":{"content":"Re-review of d85107b: five findings. The enumerat…","message":"Re-review of d85107b: five findings. The enumerated coverage list keeps drifting, so stop enumerating. Same rules (three files, text only, make check, explicit-path commit, no push).\n1+4. design.md ~1537-1541 and DESIGN.md ~12620-12623: replace the list of \"bounded rows ... and counterexample rows ... also contain both\" with: \"Only the claim-u and claim+u rows exhaust the state space with the unlocked sweep and the claim-forked exit in the slice and all sixteen switches on. Every other row whose slice contains both is bounded, a switches-off counterexample run, or a mutant, and the bounded rows do not cover every operation; the spec's results table lists them.\" Keep the no-exhaustive-chain-row / F3 depth-5 sentence.\n2. DESIGN.md ~12627-12637: do not list \"the id counter\" as not represented. List \"an id returned to the counter (the code's releaseID(false)) and the moment of consumption\" as not represented, then give the used argument as why uniqueness holds in the model.\n3. N20 premise (spec ~2912-2914, design ~1584-1585, DESIGN.md ~12632-12634): add \"and each allocates only an id not in used (d? not in used)\" to \"every operation leaves used unchanged or grows it (LcCfAlloc, LcTierBDispatch); the initialisations set it empty\".\n5. spec ~2690-2696 \"The gap that let C16 through\": add the sweep+ensure slice (Fc_w, Fc_del) to the list of slices holding the unlocked sweep: it had the sweep and the exit but was run only with switches off and found counterexamples. Verify that wording against the table rows at spec ~2437-2438 before writing it.\nReport the commit hash.","recipient":"ad95b491242ef438c","recipient_kind":"agent","summary":"Fix d85107b review: stop enumerating coverage","to":"ad95b491242ef438c","type":"message"},"tool_input_hash":"f6ab069b29ccc7950d85